About the role&nbsp; 

We're looking for a Lead Automation Engineer to own the technical delivery of UiPath automation workstreams end-to-end - from design and development through testing and deployment - working with international clients across a distributed, global delivery environment. You will own the technical execution of our broader automation strategy and lead and mentor a high-performing team of engineers. You will be the agentic architecture and delivery authority for your pod, accountable for governance, production readiness and measurable outcomes of UiPath agentic solutions. &nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

- Set and enforce UiPath development standards, architectural patterns and delivery frameworks across your team's projects, including agentic standards: agent design patterns, reusable prompt and tool libraries, evaluation thresholds and promotion criteria&nbsp; 
 - Lead, mentor, and supervise a cross-functional pod of automation engineers and business analysts, fostering a culture of technical excellence&nbsp; 
 - Review and validate solution designs, ensuring they are scalable, maintainable, and aligned with enterprise standards&nbsp; 
 - Oversee the quality of UiPath deliverables across all project stages - design, build, test, and deployment&nbsp; 
 - Own discovery, estimation and delivery of Agentic AI programmes: run use-case assessments, decide agent vs. RPA vs. API vs. human, and define the target architecture across Agent Builder, coded agents, Maestro, IXP and Integration Service&nbsp; 
 - Architect multi-agent orchestration in UiPath Maestro, including process modelling, exception and escalation design, and SLAs across agents, robots and people&nbsp; 
 - Define agentic governance with client security, risk and compliance teams: AI Trust Layer policies, LLM selection, data residency, PII handling, autonomy levels and human-in-the-loop controls&nbsp; 
 - Define production readiness and the run model for agents: observability (traces, UiPath Insights), accuracy and drift monitoring, LLM consumption cost tracking and handover to support&nbsp; 
 - Conduct rigorous code and prompt reviews and enforce robust CI/CD pipelines, establishing coding standards, automated testing frameworks (Unit, Integrated, UAT) and agent evaluation pipelines that guarantee delivery excellence and mitigate deployment risks&nbsp; 
 - Partner with clients and stakeholders to understand business objectives, identify agentic automation opportunities, and define and track agent KPIs (automation rate, accuracy, cycle time, cost per transaction) to evidence business value and ROI&nbsp; 
 - Support business development by contributing to proposals, solution and LLM consumption estimates, agentic POCs and demos, client workshops and pre-sales discussions, serving as a trusted agentic automation subject matter expert&nbsp; 
 - Act as the primary technical authority and trusted advisor, aligning business stakeholders, project managers and development teams on delivery milestones and technical risks&nbsp; 
 - Delivery expectations: accountable for on-time, on-budget, quality delivery across multiple concurrent agentic workstreams, with clear status, risk and value reporting to client and Roboyo leadership&nbsp; 
 - Take the lead on diagnosing and resolving complex technical defects, optimising performance bottlenecks, and stabilizing processes before handoff to support teams&nbsp; 
 - Stay up to date on industry trends and best practices, and continuously improve consulting service offerings&nbsp; &nbsp; 

Must Have Qualifications&nbsp; 

- 8+ years of hands-on experience in Intelligent Automation software engineering, with deep, demonstrable expertise in developing complex workflows in UiPath (UiPath Studio, Orchestrator, and REFramework)&nbsp; 
 - Proven track record operating as a Technical Lead, successfully managing, staffing, and mentoring engineering teams&nbsp; 
 - UiPath Advanced RPA Developer certification and other relevant UiPath certifications (e. g. , Automation Developer Professional, Test Automation Engineer Professional, Agentic Automation Professional, or Automation Infrastructure Engineer Professional)&nbsp; 
 - Proven track record architecting and leading at least 2 production agentic automation deliveries on UiPath (Agent Builder, Maestro, Context Grounding, IXP, Action Center), including coded agents&nbsp; 
 - Deep understanding of LLM and agent architecture trade-offs: model selection, RAG design, tool calling, MCP, multi-agent patterns, guardrails, evaluation, latency and cost&nbsp; 
 - Python proficiency sufficient to design and review coded agents (UiPath Python SDK, LangGraph)&nbsp; 
 - Understanding of Responsible AI and AI governance requirements (e. g. , EU AI Act, data privacy regulations) as they apply to autonomous agents&nbsp; 
 - Solid command of software engineering principles, including SQL databases, API integrations, and version control (Git)&nbsp; 
 - Exceptional stakeholder management and communication skills, with the proven ability to conduct technical workshops, elicit granular business requirements, and negotiate complex architectural decisions with non-technical executives&nbsp; Nice to have qualifications&nbsp; 

- Experience with UiPath Automation Cloud administration, AI Trust Layer configuration and UiPath Autopilot&nbsp; 
